  "tagline": "One hundred and one rooms and twenty villas on a seahorse-shaped island in Jumeira Bay.",
  "description": "Bvlgari Resort Dubai stands on Jumeira Bay Island, an island shaped like a seahorse, with 101 rooms and suites and 20 villas. It is a two-minute ride from the mainland over a 300-metre bridge, 25 minutes by car from Dubai International Airport, and has its own beach, marina and yacht club.\n\nThe Italian firm Antonio Citterio Patricia Viel designed the resort in the manner of the Italian Riviera, with a coral-like sunshade wrapped around the facade, oak planks recalling a ship's deck, and black granite, travertine and Bvlgari marble inside. The property faces the Arabian Gulf, with the Dubai skyline across the bay.\n\nEvery room and suite has a private balcony. Guestrooms measure 53 square metres, the Deluxe Beach View Room 55, and Junior Suites 80, with views of the skyline or the Gulf. The Executive Suite is 105 square metres, and the Bvlgari Suite 120, with a 60-square-metre terrace and a two-person hydromassage. The 20 villas stand in two rows facing the beach or the skyline, each with its own pool. They have one, two or three bedrooms at 175, 250 and 315 square metres, and the Bvlgari Villa, the largest, covers 540 square metres.\n\nIl Ristorante, Niko Romito, has held two Michelin stars in the Michelin Guide Dubai since 2022, and is the Italian restaurant of the chef whose Reale in Italy held three. The Yacht Clvb Restaurant overlooks a 46-boat harbour and serves Italian fish, with a house band on Friday and Saturday evenings and Sunday afternoons. At the Serpenti Beach Clvb, La Spiaggia serves food by day and by lantern light at night, and Il Caffè has an outdoor terrace and an open pizza oven. Dario Abbate is Executive Chef.\n\nThe Bvlgari Spa and Gymnasivm cover 1,700 square metres on the ground floor, with seven treatment rooms, a couple suite, a hammam, a 25-metre indoor pool and a vitality pool inspired by the Roman baths of Caracalla. The gym is open 24 hours. Children have the Little Gems Clvb and a pool of their own.\n\nThe resort suits travellers who want a private villa or a beach room within reach of the Burj Khalifa and the Dubai Mall.",
